.TH tkuini n 0.3 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuini
.PP
Two\-pane INI viewer: sections on the left, key/value pairs of the selected section on the right. The global section "" is shown as "(global)". Built on tclutils::tuini (requires tclutils 0.32.0+).
.CS
set w [::tkutils::tkuini::widget .w]
::tkutils::tkuini::loadText      $w iniText   ;# -> section count
::tkutils::tkuini::loadFile      $w file
::tkutils::tkuini::setData       $w data
::tkutils::tkuini::sections      $w
::tkutils::tkuini::selectSection $w section
::tkutils::tkuini::currentSection $w
::tkutils::tkuini::data          $w
::tkutils::tkuini::sectionWidget $w
::tkutils::tkuini::treeWidget    $w
.CE
.SS "Editing (0.25.0)"
.PP
Pass \fB\-editable 1\fR (default) for an edit bar (Section/Key/Value + buttons). Programmatic ops:
.CS
tkuini::setKey        $w section key value
tkuini::removeKey     $w section key
tkuini::addSection    $w section
tkuini::removeSection $w section
tkuini::toText        $w            ;# current document as INI text
tkuini::save          $w file
.CE
.PP
Files: \fBloadFile\fR reads and \fBsave\fR writes UTF\-8 with LF, whatever the system encoding (since 0.3).
.PP
With tclutils \fBtuini\fR 0.2, \fBsetKey\fR and \fBaddSection\fR raise \fB{TCLUTILS TUINI VALUE}\fR for what INI cannot hold (a line break in a value, \fB=\fR in a key, ...); the data stay unchanged. The edit bar trims key and section name and shows such an error as a message instead.
.SS "Additional exported commands"
.PP
Documented for completeness (same module, also covered by the test suite):
.CS
tkuini::count path                             ;# return the number of entries currently shown
.CE
